    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/ReviewView.tsx",
      "content": "The completion focus request has no target when the receipt refresh returns `Empty`. Recording a sale/expiration can remove the last walked trade; `reopenAndApply` then sets `empty`, and `focusNext` increments `dayFocus`, but this branch unmounts `DayCard` and renders an unfocusable `EmptyReview` that does not consume the request. Focus falls back to the document body instead of a completion summary. Give the empty summary an equivalent focus target (or retain a focusable day summary), and cover dismissing the final trade's receipt with an `Empty` refresh result.",
      "existing_code": "      {empty ? \u003cEmptyReview date={review.reviewDate} /\u003e : \u003cDayCard focus={dayFocus} review={review} name={name} openCard={openCard} openMarks={openMarks} openSkipped={openSkipped} holding={new Set([...holding, ...soldOut])} onStillHolding={stillHolding} /\u003e}",
      "start_line": 582,
      "end_line": 582,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/ReviewView.tsx",
      "content": "Guard this focus request against a changed card selection while the receipt refresh is pending. After pressing Back to the Review, the trader can open another card before `onRefresh()` resolves; the receipt callback still calls `focusNext`, which moves focus away from that newly selected card (or an input in it). `refreshTrade` already guards its shown-card updates with `selection.current`, but this callback bypasses that protection. Capture the receipt's opening/selection and only advance focus if it is still current, as the Action-save path does.",
      "existing_code": "  const focusNext = () =\u003e {\n    const held = latest.current.review;",
      "start_line": 362,
